# Line endings are PER FILE in this project and the difference is load-bearing:
# PROJECT_CONTEXT §8 records that `tests/data-validation.js` and
# `tools/generate-data.js` are CRLF while most of `src/**` and
# `tests/engine-battle.js` are LF, and that a scripted multi-line patch which
# guesses wrong silently matches nothing — which has cost real time twice, once
# in bash and once in Python.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the authoring machine, so without this git would
# store everything as LF and check it back out as CRLF on Windows / LF on macOS,
# flattening the distinction the docs tell the next person to rely on.
#
# `-text` means: never convert, in either direction. Bytes round-trip exactly.
* -text
